         # ============================================================
+        # BUG DEDUPLICATION
+        #
+        # Candidate bugs collected during the loop above are merged here:
+        # multiple failing tests that share the same module + test
+        # category + normalized failure signal become one master bug,
+        # with every occurrence preserved in that bug's `affected` list.
+        # Bugs are persisted to the DB only after this merge, so the
+        # stored bug count reflects distinct issues, not raw failures.
+        # ============================================================
+
+        bugs = deduplicate_bugs(bugs)
